# Text files are stored as LF and, importantly, checked out as LF on every
# platform — `eol=lf`, not bare `text=auto`.
#
# Prettier is configured with `"endOfLine": "lf"`. With plain `text=auto` on a
# machine where `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default), a fresh clone
# lands CRLF in the working tree and `npm run format:check` then fails on files
# nobody has touched. Pinning the checkout keeps the working tree, the repository
# and Prettier in agreement.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never transform these.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# SVG is XML, so it is text — listed only to make that explicit, since the two
# SVGs in `public/` are hand-edited source, not exported binaries.
*.svg text
